<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cyril and Methodius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">9th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Saints Cyril and Methodius</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cyril and Methodius were Byzantine Greek brothers and missionaries of the ninth century who worked among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a> of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>. They created the Glagolitic alphabet and translated liturgical texts into Old Church Slavonic. Their work laid the foundation for Slavic Christian literature and spread the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a>'s cultural influence.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cyril-and-methodius.jpg" alt="Cyril and Methodius" width="317" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: painted by Zahari Zograf (Захарий Христович Димитров) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sv_Kiril_Metodij_Zahari_Zograf_Trojanski_mon_1848.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
